1
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:09,316
Every flower starts as a tiny bud. Some take a long time to open.

2
00:00:09,716 --> 00:00:12,192
This little one? Very, very long.

3
00:00:13,492 --> 00:00:20,256
In twenty eighteen, ABS-CBN's Star Hunt Academy began training a group of young hopefuls.

4
00:00:20,656 --> 00:00:26,247
Filipino and Korean coaches drilled them in singing and dancing, again and again.

5
00:00:27,547 --> 00:00:35,612
In October twenty twenty, eight trainees graduated: Aiah, Colet, Maloi, Gwen, Stacey, Mikha, Jhoanna, and Sheena.

6
00:00:36,012 --> 00:00:41,005
Their name, BINI, comes from binibini, the Filipino word for a young lady.

7
00:00:41,405 --> 00:00:45,567
Their first song was a fresh take on the classic Da Coconut Nut.

8
00:00:46,867 --> 00:00:51,817
On June eleventh, twenty twenty-one, they officially debuted with Born to Win.

9
00:00:52,217 --> 00:00:56,208
It was the pandemic, so their first crowds were mostly on screens.

10
00:00:57,508 --> 00:01:04,379
Then, in twenty twenty-three, came Pantropiko, a sunny summer song with a dance anyone could copy.

11
00:01:04,779 --> 00:01:09,452
Soon it seemed to be everywhere: on phones, at parties, at school programs.

12
00:01:09,852 --> 00:01:15,336
BINI became known as the Nation's Girl Group, and their fans, the Blooms, kept growing.

13
00:01:16,636 --> 00:01:21,757
In April twenty twenty-six, they even performed at Coachella in California.

14
00:01:23,057 --> 00:01:28,136
So how did BINI bloom? Years of practice, eight friends, and a lot of patience.

15
00:01:28,536 --> 00:01:31,460
And the little bud? It finally opened too.
